.th MOD VIII June/77
.sh NAME
mod \*- modify documentation database
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd mod
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it mod
is used to modify the database used by
.it doc
(I).
The main use of this database is to document changes and local peculiarities
for a particular installation.
.s3
.it mod
is designed for interactive use but, since it uses standard input
and output, it can be used in more cunning ways.
.s3
.it mod
includes all the facilities available under
.it doc.
As well it supports the following commands:
.s3
.nf
	-k string = insert keyword 'string';
	-l string n = link keyword 'string' to title 'n';
	-x string n = kill link between keyword 'string' & title 'n';
	-d string or n = delete keyword 'string' or title 'n';
	-e n = edit title 'n';
	-w n = write title 'n' & abstract to file 'n';
	-? n = list keywords linked to title 'n';
	-i filename = insert title & abstract from file;
	-r filename n = replace title & abstract 'n' with file;
	carriage return = list commands;
	rubout = return to command level;
	control D = exit.
.fi
.sh FILES
.nf
.if t .ta 1.2i
.if n .ta 25
.fi
.dt
/usr/pub/keywords
.br
/usr/pub/keylinks
.br
/usr/pub/titles
.br
/usr/pub/abstracts
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
self-explanatory
.sh "SEE ALSO"
doc(I)
.sh AUTHOR
Peter Hewitt (University of New South Wales)
.sh BUGS
Command syntax analysis is primitive - core dumps have occurred.
